      "message": "To avoid the sleep-while-atomic issues, you need this hook to be a restricted hook instead of a regular one since restrict hook handlers are invoked in the context of the callsite -- w/o disabling preemption. As Saravana mentioned, the existing hook is part of the KMI and cannot be changed now, so you can accomplish this by adding the restricted hook:\n\n```\n    trace_android_vh_v4l2subdev_set_fmt(sd, subdev_fh-\u003epad,\n\t\t\t\t\tformat, \u0026ret);\n+   trace_android_rvh_v4l2subdev_set_fmt(sd, subdev_fh-\u003epad,\n+\t\t\t\t\t format, \u0026ret);\n```\n\nYour hander will now attach to the \"rvh\" version which allows for the handler to sleep.\n\nThe same approach would be taken for the other cases below.",
